# HyperSkill Quiz Backend

A Java-based quiz management backend built with **Maven**, **Hibernate ORM**, and **MySQL**.  
It serves as the backend core for a console-driven quiz system that supports multiple quiz types, persistent question storage, and dynamic retrieval.

This version is a major upgrade from the initial prototype, introducing a fully modular structure, database persistence, and clearer separation of concerns for scalability and maintainability.

---

## 🚀 Features

- **Modular Maven structure** — clean `src/main/java` organization for entities, services, and utilities  
- **Database persistence (MySQL + Hibernate)** — stores questions, choices, and quiz data for scalable management  
- **Service layer abstraction** — separates logic from data access for easier maintenance and testing  
- **Dynamic question loading** — retrieves quiz questions directly from the database  
- **Improved scalability & readability** — organized architecture following OOP and layered design  
- **Fast runtime** — ~3-second cold start due to Hibernate initialization; near-instant performance afterward  
- **Easily extensible** — new quiz types, difficulty levels, and user tracking can be added with minimal code changes

---

## 🧱 Project Structure

HyperSkill/
│
├── src/
│ ├── main/
│ │ ├── java/com/quizzes/
│ │ │ ├── Services/ # JPA entity classes, Logic Flow (Main, Questions, QuestionType, LogicFlow)
│ │ │ ├── utilities/ # Utility and helper classes (InputValidator, HibernateUtil)
│ │ │ └── Main.java # Application entry point
│ │ └── resources/
│ │ └── hibernate.cfg.xml # Hibernate configuration
│ └── test/
│
├── pom.xml # Maven dependencies and build configuration
└── README.md


