## ⚙️ Setup & Usage

### 1️⃣ Clone the repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/daikendy/HyperSkill.git
cd HyperSkill

💡 Design Highlights

From hardcoded to persistent — migrated from static Java-based question storage to a relational MySQL backend

Improved maintainability — question updates and new quiz types now require no code changes

Clear service separation — logic split into distinct services and utilities following clean architecture principles

Scalable schema — supports adding users, attempts, and results tables for advanced analytics

| Phase                        | Goal                                          | Key Additions                        |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| **1. Spring Boot Migration** | Simplify config & enable dependency injection | Spring Boot Starter, Spring Data JPA |
| **2. DB Migrations**         | Version-controlled schema                     | Flyway or Liquibase                  |
| **3. API Layer**             | Expose REST endpoints                         | `@RestController`, JSON responses    |
| **4. Observability**         | Monitoring & metrics                          | Spring Boot Actuator, Micrometer     |
| **5. Containerization**      | Portable deployment                           | Dockerfile + docker-compose          |
| **6. CI/CD Pipeline**        | Automated testing & build                     | GitHub Actions                       |
| **7. Security**              | Hardened production setup                     | Spring Security, CORS rules          |



🧪 Possible Enhancements

Add unit & integration tests using JUnit and Mockito

Integrate logging framework (SLF4J + Logback) instead of System.out.println

Implement caching (Redis or Caffeine) for high-frequency queries

Track metrics: average quiz duration, attempts per session, success rate

Add user accounts & scoring history to support leaderboards

